IMPORT prelude

-- Vermont personal income tax, 32 V.S.A. chapter 151 -- what an individual meets: who must file a Vermont return and by when
-- (s 5861(a)-(c)), paying what withholding and estimates have not (s 5871(3)), Vermont taxable income from federal adjusted
-- gross income (s 5811(21)), the Social Security exclusion (s 5830e(a)), the rate tables and the 3 percent minimum tax above
-- $150,000 of federal AGI (s 5822(a), (b)), the charitable contribution credit (s 5822(d)(3)), the part-year and nonresident
-- reduction (s 5822(e)), and the refundable credits: the earned income tax credit (s 5828b), the child and dependent care
-- credit (s 5828c) and the Vermont child tax credit (s 5830f).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer (a resident, part-year resident or nonresident individual, filing alone or jointly). "Must I
-- file? What is my Vermont taxable income? How much tax do I owe? What credits do I get back?" Provisions addressed to the
-- Commissioner (inflation adjustment, s 5811(21)(D), s 5822(b)(2)) are encoded as what they mean for that person: the amount
-- for the year is a figure the Commissioner publishes, which the person states.
--
-- Edition: Vermont Statutes Online (unofficial), including the actions of the 2026 session, fetched 2026-10-19 (UTC), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/vt-32-vsa-ch151-2026.txt.
--
-- FEDERAL INPUTS. Vermont starts from federal adjusted gross income and borrows federal credits (s 5811(21), s 5824 adopts the
-- federal income tax laws as in effect on December 31, 2025). Federal AGI, the federally taxable Social Security benefits, the
-- federal EITC, the federal child and dependent care credit and entitlement to the federal child tax credit are asked as
-- facts. The federal text and its encoding are at subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not
-- possible in the stable l4; NOTES.md names the link).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Estates and trusts (s 5822(a)(5), s 5811(28)); the itemised additions and subtractions of s 5811(21)(A) and
-- (B)(i)-(iii), (v)-(x) are asked as two totals; s 5830e(b)-(e) (retirement income other than Social Security: the s 5830e(e)
-- election is out, so Social Security is taken as the elected exclusion); s 5811(21)(C)(iv)(II) (continuing care retirement
-- community fees, taken as nil); s 5822(c), (d)(1)-(2) (federal recapture taxes, farm income averaging, the elderly or
-- disabled credit, investment credits); the credits in ss 5825-5828, 5830b-5830d, 5830g; estimated tax (subch. 5);
-- withholding (subch. 4); s 5830f(d) advance payments (effective only when a contingency is met). A part-year resident or
-- nonresident whose Vermont income is zero or negative answers `not covered` (s 5822(e) then turns on Vermont income computed
-- without the s 5823(a) reductions, which is not asked).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Vermont personal income tax -- 32 V.S.A. chapter 151`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 5822(e), second proviso
    `my Vermont income is zero or negative, and s 5822(e) then turns on my Vermont income computed without the s 5823(a) reductions, which this encoding does not ask`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `The people and the filing statuses`

-- s 5822(b)(1): "'Married individuals,' 'surviving spouse,' 'head of household,' 'unmarried individual,' ... have the same
-- meaning as under the Internal Revenue Code" (a borrowed term, asked as a fact). s 5861(c): spouses who file a joint federal
-- return "shall file a joint Vermont personal income tax return", so the federal filing status carries over.
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `married filing jointly`
    `surviving spouse`
    `head of household`
    `unmarried`                        -- "unmarried individuals (other than surviving spouse or head of household)"
    `married filing separately`

-- s 5828b, s 5828c, s 5830f, s 5822(e): residence during the taxable year.
DECLARE `Residence in the year` IS ONE OF
    `a resident all year`
    `a part-year resident`
    `a nonresident all year`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the Commissioner of Taxes`

DECLARE `Action` IS ONE OF
    `file a Vermont personal income tax return`
    `pay the tax not discharged by withholding or estimated payments`

§§ `s 5861 -- who must file, and by when`

-- s 5861(a): "Every individual ... subject to taxation for any taxable year under section 5822 of this title shall file a
-- Vermont personal income tax return for that taxable year if that person is required to file a United States income tax
-- return for that year and (1) earned or received more than $100.00 of Vermont income, or (2) earned or received more than
-- $1,000.00 in gross income from the sources listed in subdivisions 5823(b)(1) through (6) of this title, whether or not a
-- resident, in that year, or has a tax liability under this chapter for that year."
-- Read as: [required to file federally AND (VT income > $100 OR s 5823(b) gross income > $1,000)] OR a tax liability. The
-- final "or has a tax liability" is read as its own limb (NOTES.md finding 1).
GIVEN `required to file a federal return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Vermont income`                    IS A NUMBER
      `gross income from s 5823(b)(1)-(6) sources` IS A NUMBER
      `has a tax liability under chapter 151` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5861(a) duty to file applies` IF
        (    `required to file a federal return`
         AND (   `Vermont income` GREATER THAN 100
              OR `gross income from s 5823(b)(1)-(6) sources` GREATER THAN 1000))
    OR `has a tax liability under chapter 151`

-- s 5861(b): the return "shall be filed on or before the date a United States income tax return is originally required to be
-- filed ... or the date as extended by the Commissioner under section 5868". s 5871(3): "All income tax liabilities not
-- theretofore discharged by withholding or installment payments shall be paid on or before the date when the return of the
-- taxpayer for the taxable year is required to be filed." Both run to the same day; the days from the end of the taxable
-- year to the federal due date (or the extended date) are a fact. The rule is counted in days from the end of the year.
GIVEN `days to the federal due date or the extended date` IS A NUMBER
      `an unpaid balance remains`                         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to file and pay` `days to the federal due date or the extended date` `an unpaid balance remains` MEANS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `file a Vermont personal income tax return`
    WITHIN `days to the federal due date or the extended date`
    HENCE  `my duty to pay` `days to the federal due date or the extended date` `an unpaid balance remains`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "no Vermont return filed by the federal due date (32 V.S.A. s 5861(b))"

-- s 5871(3): the payment duty runs to the same day as the return. Under HENCE the deadline counts from the filing, so the
-- clock is not restarted: a balance must be paid with the return (WITHIN 0 of filing, the day itself counting).
GIVEN `days to the federal due date or the extended date` IS A NUMBER
      `an unpaid balance remains`                         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to pay` `days to the federal due date or the extended date` `an unpaid balance remains` MEANS
    IF `an unpaid balance remains`
    THEN PARTY  `the taxpayer`
         MUST   `pay the tax not discharged by withholding or estimated payments`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "tax not discharged by withholding or estimates was not paid by the return due date (32 V.S.A. s 5871(3))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s 5830e(a) -- the Social Security exclusion`

-- s 5830e(a)(1) single, married filing separately, head of household or surviving spouse: all federally taxable benefits
-- excluded at federal AGI up to $55,000; between $55,000 and $65,000, "(i) subtracting the federal adjusted gross income of the
-- taxpayer from $65,000.00; (ii) dividing ... by $10,000.00; and (iii) multiplying ... by the federally taxable benefits"; none
-- at $65,000 or more. (a)(2) married filing jointly: the same at $70,000 and $80,000.
GIVEN `filing status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5830e(a) full exclusion ceiling` `filing status` MEANS
    IF `filing status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` THEN 70000 ELSE 55000

GIVEN `filing status` IS A `Filing status`
      `federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `federally taxable Social Security benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Social Security exclusion` `filing status` `federal adjusted gross income` `federally taxable Social Security benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `federal adjusted gross income` AT MOST `ceiling`
        THEN `federally taxable Social Security benefits`
        IF `federal adjusted gross income` LESS THAN `ceiling` PLUS 10000
        THEN ((`ceiling` PLUS 10000 MINUS `federal adjusted gross income`) DIVIDED BY 10000) TIMES `federally taxable Social Security benefits`
        OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        `ceiling` MEANS `the s 5830e(a) full exclusion ceiling` `filing status`

§§ `s 5811(21) -- Vermont taxable income`

-- The amounts the Commissioner adjusts each year for inflation (s 5811(21)(D); s 5822(b)(2)). The statute prints the base
-- figures; the figures for the taxable year are published by the Commissioner and are stated by the person.
DECLARE `Amounts for the year` HAS
    `personal exemption`               IS A NUMBER   -- s 5811(21)(C)(i): $4,150.00 printed
    `standard deduction`               IS A NUMBER   -- s 5811(21)(C)(ii): $6,000 / $9,000 / $12,000 printed, by status
    `additional deduction per s 63(f) deduction` IS A NUMBER  -- s 5811(21)(C)(iii): $1,000.00 printed
    `first bracket ceiling`            IS A NUMBER   -- s 5822(a): the top of the 3.35% band for the status
    `second bracket ceiling`           IS A NUMBER   -- the top of the 6.6% band
    `third bracket ceiling`            IS A NUMBER   -- the top of the 7.6% band

-- s 5811(21)(C)(ii): "(I) ... unmarried (other than surviving spouses or heads of households) or married filing separate
-- returns, $6,000.00; (II) ... head of household, $9,000.00; and (III) ... married filing joint return or surviving spouse,
-- $12,000.00".
GIVEN `filing status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the printed standard deduction` `filing status` MEANS
    CONSIDER `filing status`
    WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN 12000
    WHEN `surviving spouse`       THEN 12000
    WHEN `head of household`      THEN 9000
    OTHERWISE 6000

-- s 5822(a)(1)-(4): the printed bracket ceilings.
GIVEN `filing status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A `Amounts for the year`
`the amounts printed in the statute` `filing status` MEANS
    `Amounts for the year` WITH
        `personal exemption`               IS 4150
        `standard deduction`               IS `the printed standard deduction` `filing status`
        `additional deduction per s 63(f) deduction` IS 1000
        `first bracket ceiling`            IS `first`
        `second bracket ceiling`           IS `second`
        `third bracket ceiling`            IS `third`
    WHERE
        `first`  MEANS CONSIDER `filing status`
                       WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN 64600
                       WHEN `surviving spouse`       THEN 64600
                       WHEN `head of household`      THEN 51850
                       WHEN `unmarried`              THEN 38700
                       OTHERWISE 32300
        `second` MEANS CONSIDER `filing status`
                       WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN 156150
                       WHEN `surviving spouse`       THEN 156150
                       WHEN `head of household`      THEN 133850
                       WHEN `unmarried`              THEN 93700
                       OTHERWISE 78075
        `third`  MEANS CONSIDER `filing status`
                       WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN 237950
                       WHEN `surviving spouse`       THEN 237950
                       WHEN `head of household`      THEN 216700
                       WHEN `unmarried`              THEN 195450
                       OTHERWISE 118975

-- s 5811(21)(C)(i): "a personal exemption ... per person for the taxpayer, for the spouse or the deceased spouse of the taxpayer
-- whose filing status ... is married filing a joint return or surviving spouse, and for each individual qualifying as a
-- dependent of the taxpayer under 26 U.S.C. s 152, provided that no exemption may be claimed for an individual who is a
-- dependent of another taxpayer". Read: the taxpayer's own exemption is lost if the taxpayer is another's dependant; the
-- spouse's if the spouse is (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN `filing status` IS A `Filing status`
      `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of my dependents under s 152` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of personal exemptions` `filing status` `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` `number of my dependents under s 152` MEANS
    `mine` PLUS `spouse's` PLUS `number of my dependents under s 152`
    WHERE
        `mine`     MEANS IF `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` THEN 0 ELSE 1
        `spouse's` MEANS IF     (`filing status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` OR `filing status` EQUALS `surviving spouse`)
                            AND NOT (`my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer`)
                         THEN 1
                         ELSE 0

DECLARE `Taxpayer` HAS
    `filing status`                                IS A `Filing status`
    `residence`                                    IS A `Residence in the year`
    `federal adjusted gross income`                IS A NUMBER
    `s 5811(21)(A) additions`                      IS A NUMBER  -- items excluded federally that Vermont adds back
    `s 5811(21)(B) subtractions other than s 5830e` IS A NUMBER -- e.g. US obligations interest, the capital gain exclusion
    `federally taxable Social Security benefits`   IS A NUMBER
    `personal exemptions claimed`                  IS A NUMBER
    `s 63(f) deductions received`                  IS A NUMBER  -- federal additional standard deductions for age 65 or blindness
    `federal medical expense deduction`            IS A NUMBER  -- itemised at the federal level under 26 U.S.C. s 213
    `Vermont income`                               IS A NUMBER  -- s 5823: for a resident all year, equal to the s 5822(e) AGI
    `charitable contributions allowable under s 170` IS A NUMBER
    `amounts`                                      IS AN `Amounts for the year`

-- s 5811(21)(B)(iv) with s 5830e(a).
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Social Security exclusion for` t MEANS
    `the Social Security exclusion` (t's `filing status`) (t's `federal adjusted gross income`) (t's `federally taxable Social Security benefits`)

-- s 5822(e): "adjusted gross income means federal adjusted gross income modified by the additions and subtractions provided for
-- in subdivisions 5811(21)(A) and (B)".
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the modified adjusted gross income of` t MEANS
    ((t's `federal adjusted gross income` PLUS t's `s 5811(21)(A) additions`)
        MINUS t's `s 5811(21)(B) subtractions other than s 5830e`) MINUS `the Social Security exclusion for` t

-- s 5811(21)(C)(iv): "an amount equal to the itemized deduction for medical expenses taken at the federal level ... (I) minus
-- the amount of the Vermont standard deduction and Vermont personal exemptions taken". Not below zero (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the medical expense deduction of` t MEANS
    max 0 (t's `federal medical expense deduction` MINUS `the standard deduction and exemptions of` t)

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard deduction and exemptions of` t MEANS
    (t's `personal exemptions claimed` TIMES t's `amounts`'s `personal exemption`) PLUS t's `amounts`'s `standard deduction`

-- s 5811(21): taxable income is federal AGI, increased by (A), decreased by (B) and by the exemptions and deductions in (C).
-- Taxable income below zero is taken as zero (the tables start at zero).
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Vermont taxable income of` t MEANS
    max 0 (`the modified adjusted gross income of` t MINUS `the deductions of` t)

-- s 5811(21)(C)(i)-(iv) together.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deductions of` t MEANS
    sum (LIST `the standard deduction and exemptions of` t,
              t's `s 63(f) deductions received` TIMES t's `amounts`'s `additional deduction per s 63(f) deduction`,
              `the medical expense deduction of` t)

§§ `s 5822 -- the tax`

-- s 5822(a)(1)-(4): 3.35% to the first ceiling; then a fixed amount plus 6.6%, 7.6% and 8.75% of the excess over each ceiling.
-- The printed fixed amounts ($2,164.00, $8,206.00, $14,423.00 for joint filers, and so on) are the tax on each ceiling at the
-- lower rates, rounded to the nearest dollar (NOTES.md finding 2); with the Commissioner's adjusted ceilings they are worked
-- out the same way.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the nearest dollar` `x` MEANS FLOOR (`x` PLUS 0.5)

GIVEN a IS AN `Amounts for the year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed amount at the first ceiling` a MEANS
    `to the nearest dollar` (a's `first bracket ceiling` TIMES 3.35%)

GIVEN a IS AN `Amounts for the year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed amount at the second ceiling` a MEANS
    `to the nearest dollar` ((a's `first bracket ceiling` TIMES 3.35%)
                             PLUS ((a's `second bracket ceiling` MINUS a's `first bracket ceiling`) TIMES 6.6%))

GIVEN a IS AN `Amounts for the year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed amount at the third ceiling` a MEANS
    `to the nearest dollar` ((a's `first bracket ceiling` TIMES 3.35%)
                             PLUS ((a's `second bracket ceiling` MINUS a's `first bracket ceiling`) TIMES 6.6%)
                             PLUS ((a's `third bracket ceiling` MINUS a's `second bracket ceiling`) TIMES 7.6%))

GIVEN a IS AN `Amounts for the year`
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the table tax` a `taxable income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `taxable income` AT MOST a's `first bracket ceiling`
        THEN `taxable income` TIMES 3.35%
        IF `taxable income` AT MOST a's `second bracket ceiling`
        THEN `the fixed amount at the first ceiling` a PLUS ((`taxable income` MINUS a's `first bracket ceiling`) TIMES 6.6%)
        IF `taxable income` AT MOST a's `third bracket ceiling`
        THEN `the fixed amount at the second ceiling` a PLUS ((`taxable income` MINUS a's `second bracket ceiling`) TIMES 7.6%)
        OTHERWISE `the fixed amount at the third ceiling` a PLUS ((`taxable income` MINUS a's `third bracket ceiling`) TIMES 8.75%)

-- s 5822(a)(6): "If the federal adjusted gross income of the taxpayer exceeds $150,000.00, then the tax calculated under this
-- subsection shall be the greater of the tax calculated under subdivisions (1)-(5) of this subsection or three percent of the
-- taxpayer's federal adjusted gross income."
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5822(a) tax of` t MEANS
    IF t's `federal adjusted gross income` GREATER THAN 150000
    THEN max `table` (t's `federal adjusted gross income` TIMES 3%)
    ELSE `table`
    WHERE
        `table` MEANS `the table tax` (t's `amounts`) (`the Vermont taxable income of` t)

-- s 5822(d)(3): "a nonrefundable charitable contribution credit ... five percent of the first $20,000.00 in charitable
-- contributions made during the taxable year that are allowable under 26 U.S.C. s 170 ... irrespective of a taxpayer's
-- election not to itemize at the federal level."
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the charitable contribution credit of` t MEANS
    min (min 20000 (t's `charitable contributions allowable under s 170`) TIMES 5%) (`the s 5822(a) tax of` t)

-- s 5822(e): "The tax determined under subsections (a) through (d) of this section shall be reduced by a percentage equal to
-- the portion of adjusted gross income that is not Vermont income; provided, however, that if a taxpayer's Vermont income
-- exceeds the taxpayer's adjusted gross income, no reduction shall be made and ... if a taxpayer has zero or negative Vermont
-- income and the taxpayer's Vermont income computed without regard to the reductions in subsection 5823(a) ... does not equal
-- or exceed the taxpayer's adjusted gross income, no tax shall be due".
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the Vermont income tax of` t MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF t's `Vermont income` AT MOST 0 AND NOT (t's `residence` EQUALS `a resident all year`)
        THEN `not covered` `my Vermont income is zero or negative, and s 5822(e) then turns on my Vermont income computed without the s 5823(a) reductions, which this encoding does not ask`
        IF t's `Vermont income` AT LEAST `agi` OR `agi` AT MOST 0
        THEN `answered` `before (e)`
        OTHERWISE `answered` (`before (e)` TIMES (t's `Vermont income` DIVIDED BY `agi`))
    WHERE
        `agi`        MEANS `the modified adjusted gross income of` t
        `before (e)` MEANS `the s 5822(a) tax of` t MINUS `the charitable contribution credit of` t

§§ `ss 5828b, 5828c, 5830f -- the refundable credits`

-- The part-year resident's share in ss 5828b, 5828c and 5830f: "the percentage that the individual's income that is earned or
-- received during the period of the individual's residency in this State bears to the individual's total income". A resident
-- all year takes 100 percent; a nonresident all year has no credit (each section is for a "resident individual or part-year
-- resident individual").
GIVEN `residence` IS A `Residence in the year`
      `income while resident` IS A NUMBER
      `total income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residency share` `residence` `income while resident` `total income` MEANS
    CONSIDER `residence`
    WHEN `a resident all year`    THEN 1
    WHEN `a nonresident all year` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE IF `total income` AT MOST 0 THEN 0 ELSE `income while resident` DIVIDED BY `total income`

-- s 5828b(a): "38 percent [for an individual who claims one or more qualifying children] or ... 100 percent [for one who does
-- not] of the earned income tax credit granted to the individual under the laws of the United States, multiplied by the
-- percentage" above. An individual who would have had the federal credit but for a missing taxpayer identification number "shall
-- be entitled to a credit under this section"; that individual states the federal credit they would have had.
-- s 5828b(b): the excess over tax "shall be paid to the taxpayer" (refundable).
GIVEN `federal earned income tax credit` IS A NUMBER
      `I claim one or more qualifying children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `residency share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Vermont earned income tax credit` `federal earned income tax credit` `I claim one or more qualifying children` `residency share` MEANS
    `federal earned income tax credit` TIMES `percentage` TIMES `residency share`
    WHERE
        `percentage` MEANS IF `I claim one or more qualifying children` THEN 38% ELSE 100%

-- s 5828c: "a refundable credit ... equal to 72 percent of the federal child and dependent care credit allowed", times the
-- residency share for a part-year resident.
GIVEN `federal child and dependent care credit` IS A NUMBER
      `residency share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Vermont child and dependent care credit` `federal child and dependent care credit` `residency share` MEANS
    `federal child and dependent care credit` TIMES 72% TIMES `residency share`

-- s 5830f(a): "$1,000.00 per qualifying child, as defined under 26 U.S.C. s 152(c) ... who is six years of age or younger as of
-- the close of the calendar year". (b): "reduced, but not below zero, by $20.00 for each $1,000.00, or fraction thereof, by which
-- the individual's adjusted gross income exceeds $125,000.00, irrespective of the individual's filing status. ... spouses filing
-- jointly shall be considered an individual." The adjusted gross income in (b) is read as federal AGI (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5830f(b) reduction per child` `adjusted gross income` MEANS
    IF `adjusted gross income` AT MOST 125000
    THEN 0
    ELSE 20 TIMES CEILING ((`adjusted gross income` MINUS 125000) DIVIDED BY 1000)

GIVEN `I am entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be but for a missing taxpayer identification number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualifying children aged six or younger at the close of the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `residency share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Vermont child tax credit` `I am entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be but for a missing taxpayer identification number` `qualifying children aged six or younger at the close of the calendar year` `adjusted gross income` `residency share` MEANS
    IF `I am entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be but for a missing taxpayer identification number`
    THEN (`qualifying children aged six or younger at the close of the calendar year` TIMES `the credit per child`) TIMES `residency share`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the credit per child` MEANS max 0 (1000 MINUS `the s 5830f(b) reduction per child` `adjusted gross income`)

§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

§§ `Must I file a Vermont return?`

@export Must I file a Vermont personal income tax return for the year (32 V.S.A. s 5861(a))?
GIVEN `I am required to file a federal income tax return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you must file a United States income tax return for the same taxable year
      `my Vermont income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Vermont income for the year in US dollars: for a resident all year, your federal adjusted gross income with the Vermont adjustments; for a nonresident, only income from Vermont sources (32 V.S.A. s 5823)
      `my gross income from Vermont rents, property sales, work, business, deferred pay or wagering` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross income in US dollars from the Vermont sources listed in 32 V.S.A. s 5823(b)(1)-(6): rents and royalties from Vermont property, gains on Vermont property, pay for work done in Vermont, a business carried on in Vermont, deferred pay earned there, and Vermont wagering or lottery winnings
      `I have a Vermont income tax liability for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owe any Vermont income tax under chapter 151 for the year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a Vermont return` IF
    `the s 5861(a) duty to file applies` `I am required to file a federal income tax return for the year` `my Vermont income` `my gross income from Vermont rents, property sales, work, business, deferred pay or wagering` `I have a Vermont income tax liability for the year`

@export Must my spouse and I file a joint Vermont return (32 V.S.A. s 5861(c))?
GIVEN `we file a joint federal return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your spouse (or you as a surviving spouse) file a joint United States income tax return for the year
      `the Commissioner allows a different filing status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Vermont Commissioner of Taxes has allowed you a different filing status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we file a joint Vermont return` IF
    `we file a joint federal return for the year` AND NOT (`the Commissioner allows a different filing status`)

§§ `How much Vermont tax do I owe?`

-- The seat's plain inputs, built into a `Taxpayer` record.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `residence` IS A `Residence in the year`, `agi` IS A NUMBER, `additions` IS A NUMBER, `subtractions` IS A NUMBER, `ss benefits` IS A NUMBER, `dependent` IS A BOOLEAN, `spouse dependent` IS A BOOLEAN, `dependents` IS A NUMBER, `s63f` IS A NUMBER, `medical` IS A NUMBER, `vt income` IS A NUMBER, `charity` IS A NUMBER, `exemption` IS A NUMBER, `standard` IS A NUMBER, `extra` IS A NUMBER, `c1` IS A NUMBER, `c2` IS A NUMBER, `c3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxpayer`
`the taxpayer with` `status` `residence` `agi` `additions` `subtractions` `ss benefits` `dependent` `spouse dependent` `dependents` `s63f` `medical` `vt income` `charity` `exemption` `standard` `extra` `c1` `c2` `c3` MEANS
    `Taxpayer` WITH
        `filing status`                                 IS `status`
        `residence`                                     IS `residence`
        `federal adjusted gross income`                 IS `agi`
        `s 5811(21)(A) additions`                       IS `additions`
        `s 5811(21)(B) subtractions other than s 5830e` IS `subtractions`
        `federally taxable Social Security benefits`    IS `ss benefits`
        `personal exemptions claimed`                   IS `the number of personal exemptions` `status` `dependent` `spouse dependent` `dependents`
        `s 63(f) deductions received`                   IS `s63f`
        `federal medical expense deduction`             IS `medical`
        `Vermont income`                                IS `vt income`
        `charitable contributions allowable under s 170` IS `charity`
        `amounts`                                       IS `Amounts for the year` WITH
                                                              `personal exemption`               IS `exemption`
                                                              `standard deduction`               IS `standard`
                                                              `additional deduction per s 63(f) deduction` IS `extra`
                                                              `first bracket ceiling`            IS `c1`
                                                              `second bracket ceiling`           IS `c2`
                                                              `third bracket ceiling`            IS `c3`

@export How much of my federally taxable Social Security benefits does Vermont exclude from my taxable income (32 V.S.A. s 5830e(a))?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status, the same as on your federal return: married filing jointly, surviving spouse, head of household, unmarried, or married filing separately
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income for the year in US dollars (joint, if you file jointly)
      `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of your Social Security benefits that is taxable on your federal return, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my Social Security does Vermont exclude` `my filing status` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` MEANS
    `the Social Security exclusion` `my filing status` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my federally taxable Social Security benefits`

@export What is my Vermont taxable income (32 V.S.A. s 5811(21))?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status, the same as on your federal return: married filing jointly, surviving spouse, head of household, unmarried, or married filing separately
      `my residence` IS A `Residence in the year` @desc Whether you were a Vermont resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income for the year in US dollars (joint, if you file jointly)
      `my Vermont additions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in US dollars, of income Vermont adds back under 32 V.S.A. s 5811(21)(A): interest on other states' bonds, bonus depreciation, and the other listed items; 0 if none
      `my Vermont subtractions other than Social Security` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in US dollars, of income Vermont subtracts under 32 V.S.A. s 5811(21)(B) other than the Social Security exclusion: interest on US government bonds, the capital gain exclusion, and the other listed items; 0 if none
      `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of your Social Security benefits that is taxable on your federal return, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else can claim you as a dependent
      `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else can claim your spouse as a dependent (answer no if you do not file jointly)
      `the number of my dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people qualify as your dependents under 26 U.S.C. s 152
      `my federal additional standard deductions for age or blindness` IS A NUMBER @desc How many additional standard deductions for being 65 or older or blind (26 U.S.C. s 63(f)) you and your spouse received on the federal return
      `my federal medical expense deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The itemised deduction for medical expenses you took on the federal return, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `the personal exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Vermont personal exemption for the year as adjusted by the Commissioner of Taxes; the statute prints 4150
      `the standard deduction for my status for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Vermont standard deduction for your filing status for the year as adjusted by the Commissioner of Taxes; the statute prints 6000 (unmarried or married filing separately), 9000 (head of household), 12000 (joint or surviving spouse)
      `the additional deduction for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Vermont additional deduction for each federal age or blindness deduction, as adjusted by the Commissioner of Taxes; the statute prints 1000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Vermont taxable income` `my filing status` `my residence` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my Vermont additions` `my Vermont subtractions other than Social Security` `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` `the number of my dependents` `my federal additional standard deductions for age or blindness` `my federal medical expense deduction` `the personal exemption for the year` `the standard deduction for my status for the year` `the additional deduction for the year` MEANS
    `the Vermont taxable income of` (`the taxpayer with` `my filing status` `my residence` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my Vermont additions` `my Vermont subtractions other than Social Security` `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` `the number of my dependents` `my federal additional standard deductions for age or blindness` `my federal medical expense deduction` 0 0 `the personal exemption for the year` `the standard deduction for my status for the year` `the additional deduction for the year` 0 0 0)

@export How much Vermont income tax do I owe before the refundable credits (32 V.S.A. s 5822)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status, the same as on your federal return: married filing jointly, surviving spouse, head of household, unmarried, or married filing separately
      `my residence` IS A `Residence in the year` @desc Whether you were a Vermont resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income for the year in US dollars (joint, if you file jointly)
      `my Vermont additions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in US dollars, of income Vermont adds back under 32 V.S.A. s 5811(21)(A); 0 if none
      `my Vermont subtractions other than Social Security` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in US dollars, of income Vermont subtracts under 32 V.S.A. s 5811(21)(B) other than the Social Security exclusion; 0 if none
      `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of your Social Security benefits that is taxable on your federal return, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else can claim you as a dependent
      `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else can claim your spouse as a dependent (answer no if you do not file jointly)
      `the number of my dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people qualify as your dependents under 26 U.S.C. s 152
      `my federal additional standard deductions for age or blindness` IS A NUMBER @desc How many additional standard deductions for being 65 or older or blind (26 U.S.C. s 63(f)) you and your spouse received on the federal return
      `my federal medical expense deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The itemised deduction for medical expenses you took on the federal return, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my Vermont income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Vermont income in US dollars under 32 V.S.A. s 5823; for a resident all year, enter your federal adjusted gross income with the Vermont additions and subtractions
      `my charitable contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your charitable contributions for the year allowable under 26 U.S.C. s 170, in US dollars, whether or not you itemise
      `the personal exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Vermont personal exemption for the year as adjusted by the Commissioner of Taxes; the statute prints 4150
      `the standard deduction for my status for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Vermont standard deduction for your filing status for the year as adjusted by the Commissioner; the statute prints 6000, 9000 (head of household) or 12000 (joint or surviving spouse)
      `the additional deduction for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Vermont additional deduction for each federal age or blindness deduction, as adjusted by the Commissioner; the statute prints 1000
      `the first bracket ceiling for my status` IS A NUMBER @desc The top of the 3.35 percent band for your filing status for the year as adjusted by the Commissioner; the statute prints 64600 (joint or surviving spouse), 51850 (head of household), 38700 (unmarried), 32300 (married filing separately)
      `the second bracket ceiling for my status` IS A NUMBER @desc The top of the 6.6 percent band for your status, as adjusted; the statute prints 156150, 133850, 93700 or 78075
      `the third bracket ceiling for my status` IS A NUMBER @desc The top of the 7.6 percent band for your status, as adjusted; the statute prints 237950, 216700, 195450 or 118975
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Vermont income tax do I owe` `my filing status` `my residence` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my Vermont additions` `my Vermont subtractions other than Social Security` `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` `the number of my dependents` `my federal additional standard deductions for age or blindness` `my federal medical expense deduction` `my Vermont income` `my charitable contributions` `the personal exemption for the year` `the standard deduction for my status for the year` `the additional deduction for the year` `the first bracket ceiling for my status` `the second bracket ceiling for my status` `the third bracket ceiling for my status` MEANS
    `the Vermont income tax of` (`the taxpayer with` `my filing status` `my residence` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my Vermont additions` `my Vermont subtractions other than Social Security` `my federally taxable Social Security benefits` `I am a dependent of another taxpayer` `my spouse is a dependent of another taxpayer` `the number of my dependents` `my federal additional standard deductions for age or blindness` `my federal medical expense deduction` `my Vermont income` `my charitable contributions` `the personal exemption for the year` `the standard deduction for my status for the year` `the additional deduction for the year` `the first bracket ceiling for my status` `the second bracket ceiling for my status` `the third bracket ceiling for my status`)

§§ `What credits do I get back?`

@export How much is my Vermont earned income tax credit (32 V.S.A. s 5828b), paid to me where it exceeds my tax?
GIVEN `my residence` IS A `Residence in the year` @desc Whether you were a Vermont resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `my federal earned income tax credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal earned income tax credit for the year in US dollars, or the federal credit you would have had but for a missing taxpayer identification number for you, your spouse or a child
      `I claim one or more qualifying children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim one or more qualifying children for the federal earned income tax credit
      `my income while a Vermont resident` IS A NUMBER @desc For a part-year resident, your income earned or received while you lived in Vermont, in US dollars (ignored otherwise)
      `my total income` IS A NUMBER @desc For a part-year resident, your total income for the year, in US dollars (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my Vermont earned income tax credit` `my residence` `my federal earned income tax credit` `I claim one or more qualifying children` `my income while a Vermont resident` `my total income` MEANS
    `the Vermont earned income tax credit` `my federal earned income tax credit` `I claim one or more qualifying children` (`the residency share` `my residence` `my income while a Vermont resident` `my total income`)

@export How much is my Vermont child tax credit (32 V.S.A. s 5830f), a refundable credit for each child aged six or younger?
GIVEN `my residence` IS A `Residence in the year` @desc Whether you were a Vermont resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `I am entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be but for a missing taxpayer identification number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be except that you or your spouse has no taxpayer identification number
      `my qualifying children aged six or younger` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your qualifying children (26 U.S.C. s 152(c)) are six or younger at the end of the calendar year, whether or not they have a taxpayer identification number
      `my adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income for the year in US dollars (joint, if you file jointly)
      `my income while a Vermont resident` IS A NUMBER @desc For a part-year resident, your income earned or received while you lived in Vermont, in US dollars (ignored otherwise)
      `my total income` IS A NUMBER @desc For a part-year resident, your total income for the year, in US dollars (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my Vermont child tax credit` `my residence` `I am entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be but for a missing taxpayer identification number` `my qualifying children aged six or younger` `my adjusted gross income` `my income while a Vermont resident` `my total income` MEANS
    `the Vermont child tax credit` `I am entitled to the federal child tax credit, or would be but for a missing taxpayer identification number` `my qualifying children aged six or younger` `my adjusted gross income` (`the residency share` `my residence` `my income while a Vermont resident` `my total income`)

@export How much is my Vermont child and dependent care credit (32 V.S.A. s 5828c), a refundable credit?
GIVEN `my residence` IS A `Residence in the year` @desc Whether you were a Vermont resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `my federal child and dependent care credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal child and dependent care credit allowed to you for the year, in US dollars
      `my income while a Vermont resident` IS A NUMBER @desc For a part-year resident, your income earned or received while you lived in Vermont, in US dollars (ignored otherwise)
      `my total income` IS A NUMBER @desc For a part-year resident, your total income for the year, in US dollars (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my Vermont child and dependent care credit` `my residence` `my federal child and dependent care credit` `my income while a Vermont resident` `my total income` MEANS
    `the Vermont child and dependent care credit` `my federal child and dependent care credit` (`the residency share` `my residence` `my income while a Vermont resident` `my total income`)
